  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "8d9bf4a958d3249280bb9ddb341d316babbd1e11",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3140130982,
          "type": null,
          "body": "As for futher improvements in GUI/2-pass; the File Capture window does calculate first and last timestamps, but does not store this in memory anywhere.\nThe capture_file struct currently holds the elapsed time, but does not store the first and last timestamps anywhere, and additionally the wtap_dumper or the dump functions does not seem to have access. So, during calculation of the elapsed time the first and last timestamps could be stored, and the metadata then copied over to wtap_dumper.\n\nFor improvements in single step conversion, currently it does not seem like any wtap dump implementations are utilizing any config files/profiles, but this could be a method to override the default (currently proposed at 1 second in this merge request).\nI do see the need on the horizon for configurable interface name -> channel id mappings for the blf output, so this could be something to look at after that change has been done.",
          "author": {
            "id": 20130475,
            "username": "PatrikThunstrom",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Patrik Thunström",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
